es_otherwise_keep_the_current_bar_run_a_smaller_corrected_trial_or_defer"],"scenario":"You eat one or two squares of dark chocolate most evenings and wonder whether replacing a roughly two-dollar supermarket bar with a ten-to-twelve-dollar craft bean-to-bar habit would produce a taste improvement worth the recurring premium. Those dollar figures are your budget anchors, not verified current offers. The frozen shopping set contains five exact listings: a 25.45-dollar twelve-pack of 3.30-ounce DOVE dark bars; a 30-dollar twelve-pack of 3.5-ounce Lindt 70-percent bars; one 8.99-dollar 100-gram Ritter Sport 74-percent bar; a 21.99-dollar three-pack of 100-gram Green & Black 70-percent bars; and a 14.95-dollar three-pack of 1.8-ounce Raaka coconut-milk 60-percent bars carrying bean-to-bar, small-batch, single-origin, organic and direct-source claims. The Raaka title implies 5.4 ounces across three bars while Product Dimensions reports 1.8 ounces. Background sources discuss bean-to-bar production control, cocoa-solids terminology, subjective bulk-versus-flavor cocoa classifications, Fairtrade price support, analytical versus affective sensory testing, nine-point hedonic liking, and blinding. Three community pages contain only scoped anecdotes about a bar-or-two daily habit, six varied dark bars sent as a gift, and one author's Aldi price-and-quality favorites. No source supplies a matched blind taste result, verified current labels and delivered prices, or a universal price at which quality stops improving.","target":"Audit what every frozen seller, concept and community source can and cannot establish about a daily dark-chocolate price ladder. Build an exact-offer table with literal pack, mass, price, percentage, recipe, process, ethics, rating and unknown fields; show conditional unit-price arithmetic; and identify which bars are actually comparable. Explain why bean-to-bar, Fairtrade, cocoa percentage, cocoa-solids terminology, bean class, ratings and anecdotes cannot establish a universal taste or quality breakpoint. Then design the smallest practical repeated within-person test that masks brand, package, price and marketing, randomizes equal coded portions, records unblinding, and scores detectable difference separately from nine-point liking and willingness to pay. State the current-label, allergen and offer checks and predeclared stops required before tasting. End with a person-specific next-tier stop rule and a lowest-cost passing purchase, keep-current-bar, corrected-trial or deferral outcome without health claims or a universal market cutoff."},"graph_motif":"multi_branch_synthesis","graph_node_to_step_id":{"bridge_blinded_difference_liking_protocol":"B1","bridge_cocoa_composition_quality_boundary":"B2","bridge_community_habit_value_scope":"B3","bridge_comparable_form_price_ladder":"B4","bridge_person_specific_price_stop_rule":"B7","bridge_price_ladder_decision_preparation":"B8","bridge_process_ethics_label_boundary":"B5","bridge_seller_price_pack_normalization":"B6","decision_evidence_bounded_price_ladder":"D1","prop_aldi_value_anecdote_scope":"E1","prop_bean_to_bar_process_scope":"E2","prop_blinding_bias_scope":"E3","prop_bulk_cocoa_subjective_scope":"E4","prop_cocoa_solids_definition_scope":"E5","prop_daily_habit_anecdote_scope":"E6","prop_dove_pack_price_scope":"E7","prop_fairtrade_price_support_scope":"E8","prop_green_black_pack_price_scope":"E9","prop_hedonic_liking_scale_scope":"E10","prop_lindt_pack_price_scope":"E11","prop_raaka_pack_identity_conflict_scope":"E12","prop_ritter_single_price_scope":"E13","prop_sensory_difference_liking_scope":"E14","prop_variety_gift_anecdote_scope":"E15"},"motif_compilation_schema":"graph_motif_compilation_v1","topology_checks":{"has_multiple_independent_branches":true,"has_synthesized_decision":true}},"directly_scorable_gold":false,"discovery_parameters":{"max_expansion_depth":3,"per_stratum":1,"selection_seed":"dra-v3-strata-v1"},"graph_stamp":"evidence-graph-v1:sha256:e51d1df1a2